  "goodToKnow": "Die Anstalt means institution. In older usage it meant an asylum or prison: Heilanstalt, Strafanstalt. Today it has a negative ring in that sense, but it's neutral in legal language: öffentlich-rechtliche Rundfunkanstalten are public broadcasters, and Bundesanstalt is a federal agency. In the plural it appears in the idiom Anstalten machen: Er machte Anstalten zu gehen (he was about to leave)."
